====================================================================================================
8. THE DIFFERENCING INSTRUMENT -- BUILT, RUN, AND REJECTED. Its evidence, in full.
====================================================================================================

  The design: two processes per arm per round, Q = --cells <the first cell only>,
  P = --cells <the four>. P - Q is exactly the nine large base rows; every unconditional
  row, every variant row and the R3 warm-up row is in BOTH and cancels, which would make
  the differenced quantity like-for-like even across a row-adding pair. Both processes'
  FIRST solve is the same row in the same position -- the asymmetry that sank fix1's I4.

  arm  task   P-rows  Q-rows  P-Q rows      med(P-Q) instructions   spread of Q over 5
  a01   base       15       6         9         51,738,400,192   2.23e-01
  a02   T8.1       15       6         9         52,393,486,662   2.24e-01
  a03   T8.2       19      10         9         52,502,347,153   8.27e-02
  a04   T8.3       19      10         9         52,036,060,715   1.03e-01
  a05   T8.4       21      12         9         52,973,117,914   1.83e-01
  a06   T8.5       23      14         9         52,556,027,347   2.24e-01
  a07   T8.6       23      14         9         52,374,445,400   2.36e-01
  a08   T8.7       23      14         9         52,672,248,814   2.42e-01
  a09   T8.7b      23      14         9         52,768,165,485   2.35e-01
  a10   T8.8       23      14         9         52,513,611,886   3.77e-02
  a11   T8.9       25      16         9         53,222,435,011   9.71e-02

  P - Q IS 9 ROWS AT EVERY ARM, so the construction did what it was built to do.
  WHAT REJECTS IT is the last column: the Q process's own instruction count scatters by
  15-22 %% round to round, while the P process at the later arms is reproducible to under
  0.2 %%. The rows Q contains are in P too -- so those rows DO NOT COST THE SAME inside a
  process that goes on to run nine large solves as they do in a process that does not.
  The cancellation the instrument depends on is therefore not exact, and the differenced
  steps below carry a floor larger than anything they were built to resolve:

    T8.1   differenced step  1.012662
    T8.2   differenced step  1.002078
    T8.3   differenced step  0.991119
    T8.4   differenced step  1.018008
    T8.5   differenced step  0.992126
    T8.6   differenced step  0.996545
    T8.7   differenced step  1.005686
    T8.7b  differenced step  1.001821
    T8.8   differenced step  0.995176
    T8.9   differenced step  1.013498

  The control arm T8.1 -- true step exactly zero -- reads a differenced step far from 1,
  which is the whole verdict on this instrument. IT IS REPORTED, NOT USED. Its raw data
  is retained in raw/diff/ as data, and the P process it produced IS used above, on its
  own, as the five-round whole-process sample.

